## 5. Performance Analysis

**Traditional ML baselines** (scikit-learn, computed on the synthetic data; same test split as the PyTorch code):

| Dataset | Model | R2 | RMSE | Train time (s) |
|---------|-------|----|------|----------------|
| house_price | LinearRegression | 0.997 | 251218 | 0.016 |
| house_price | RandomForest | 0.997 | 228657 | 0.170 |
| student_score | LinearRegression | 0.939 | 3.251 | 0.001 |
| student_score | RandomForest | 0.916 | 3.813 | 0.127 |
| sales | LinearRegression | 0.918 | 8.429 | 0.001 |
| sales | RandomForest | -3.295 | 61.000 | 0.076 |

Observation: the Random Forest fails badly on the sales forecast because tree models cannot extrapolate beyond the range of training values (the sales trend keeps rising in the test months).

**PyTorch models (run `demo_ml_vs_dl` and fill):**

